{'symbol': 'ABT', 'date': '2020-05-11 11:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Abbott Receives FDA Emergency Use Authorization For Covid-19 Antibody Blood Test On Alinity™ I System', 'text': 'ABBOTT RECEIVES FDA EMERGENCY USE AUTHORIZATION FOR COVID-19 ANTIBODY BLOOD TEST ON ALINITY™ I SYSTEM.ABBOTT LABORATORIES -.ABBOTT - DATA SHOWS RELIABLE RESULTS WITH 99.6% SPECIFICITY AND 100% SENSITIVITY FOR PATIENTS TESTED 14 DAYS AFTER SYMPTOMS BEGAN.ABBOTT LABORATORIES - ABBOTT PLANS TO SHIP NEARLY 30 MILLION ANTIBODY TESTS GLOBALLY IN MAY ACROSS ITS ARCHITECT AND ALINITY I PLATFORMS.ABBOTT - WILL HAVE CAPACITY TO SHIP 60 MILLION ANTIBODY TESTS IN JUNE.ABBOTT - EXPECTS TO SUBMIT FOR CE MARK FOR ITS ALINITY I SARS-COV-2 IGG TEST THIS WEEK.'}{'symbol': 'AMZN', 'date': '2020-05-11 06:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Morrisons, Amazon Announce Expansion Of Prime Now Grocery Delivery', 'text': 'MORRISONS AND AMAZON ANNOUNCE EXPANSION OF PRIME NOW GROCERY DELIVERY.MORRISONS SAYS CO, AMAZON ARE EXPANDING SAME-DAY, ONLINE GROCERY DELIVERY SERVICE TO PRIME MEMBERS, COVERING MOST OF LONDON AND MORE CITIES ACROSS UK.'}{'symbol': 'BA', 'date': '2020-05-11 23:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'BOC Aviation Says Unit To Purchase 10 Boeing 737-8 Aircraft From Southwest Airlines Co', 'text': 'BOC AVIATION- UNIT TO PURCHASE 10 BOEING 737-8 AIRCRAFT FROM SOUTHWEST AIRLINES CO.'}{'symbol': 'CAH', 'date': '2020-05-11 10:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Cardinal Health Reports Q3 Results For Fiscal Year 2020', 'text': 'CARDINAL HEALTH REPORTS THIRD QUARTER RESULTS FOR FISCAL YEAR 2020.REAFFIRMS FY 2020 NON-GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $5.20 TO $5.40.Q3 REVENUE $39.2 BILLION VERSUS REFINITIV IBES ESTIMATE OF $36.95 BILLION.Q3 GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.19.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $1.43 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.COMPANY REAFFIRMS FY20 GUIDANCE.Q3 REVENUE FOR PHARMACEUTICAL SEGMENT INCREASED 12 PERCENT TO $35.1 BILLION.CARDINAL HEALTH - EXPECTS SIGNIFICANT NET NEGATIVE IMPACT TO Q4 FINANCIAL RESULTS IN BOTH SEGMENTS.QTRLY ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE $\t $1.62.'}{'symbol': 'DXCM', 'date': '2020-05-11 10:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Dexcom Reports Proposed Offering Of $850.0 Million Of Convertible Senior Notes', 'text': 'DEXCOM ANNOUNCES PROPOSED OFFERING OF $850.0 MILLION OF CONVERTIBLE SENIOR NOTES.DEXCOM INC - TO OFFER $850.0 MILLION OF CONVERTIBLE SENIOR NOTES DUE 2025 IN A PRIVATE PLACEMENT.'}{'symbol': 'DD', 'date': '2020-05-11 11:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'International Flavors & Fragrances Reports Additional Director Appointees', 'text': 'INTERNATIONAL FLAVORS & FRAGRANCES INC - ANNOUNCES ADDITIONAL DIRECTOR APPOINTEES FOR FUTURE BOARD OF DIRECTORS.INTERNATIONAL FLAVORS & FRAGRANCES INC - COMPANIES CONTINUE TO EXPECT THAT TRANSACTION WILL CLOSE IN Q1 OF 2021..INTERNATIONAL FLAVORS & FRAGRANCES - ORGANIZATION WILL INCLUDE FOUR DIVISIONS: TASTE, FOOD & BEVERAGE,  SCENT, HEALTH & BIOSCIENCES PHARMA, SOLUTIONS.INTERNATIONAL FLAVORS & FRAGRANCES INC - MATTHIAS HEINZEL WILL BE APPOINTED TO JOIN BOARD OF DIRECTORS OF IFF.INTERNATIONAL FLAVORS & FRAGRANCES INC - CAROL DAVIDSON WILL ALSO BE APPOINTED TO JOIN BOARD OF DIRECTORS OF FUTURE COMBINED COMPANY.'}{'symbol': 'ETR', 'date': '2020-05-11 10:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Entergy Reports First Quarter Earnings', 'text': 'ENTERGY REPORTS FIRST QUARTER EARNINGS.Q1 EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.59.Q1 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $0.92 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.ENTERGY AFFIRMS 2020 ADJUSTED EPS GUIDANCE OF $5.45 TO $5.75.QTRLY ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.14.FY2020 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $5.53 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.'}{'symbol': 'GIS', 'date': '2020-05-11 10:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'General Mills Says Co Experienced Unprecedented Increase In Consumer Demand For Food At Home In March', 'text': 'GENERAL MILLS PROVIDES OPERATIONAL UPDATE AND RAISES FISCAL 2020 OUTLOOK.GENERAL MILLS - TO DATE, ALL  MANUFACTURING & DISTRIBUTION FACILITIES HAVE CONTINUED TO OPERATE WITHOUT SIGNIFICANT DISRUPTION RELATED TO COVID-19.GENERAL MILLS - IN MARCH, EXPERIENCED UNPRECEDENTED INCREASE IN CONSUMER DEMAND FOR FOOD AT HOME.GENERAL MILLS - WHILE MAGNITUDE OF INCREASED AT-HOME FOOD DEMAND MODERATED IN APRIL, REMAINED SIGNIFICANTLY ELEVATED COMPARED TO PRE-COVID-19 LEVELS.GENERAL MILLS - IN CONTRAST, HAS SEEN A SUBSTANTIAL DECLINE IN AWAY-FROM-HOME FOOD DEMAND SINCE ONSET OF PANDEMIC.GENERAL MILLS - RAISED FINANCIAL EXPECTATIONS FOR Q4 OF FISCAL 2020 TO REFLECT STRONGER THAN ANTICIPATED AT-HOME FOOD DEMAND IN MARCH AND APRIL.GENERAL MILLS INC - EXPECTS Q4 ORGANIC NET SALES TO INCREASE DOUBLE DIGITS VERSUS PRIOR YEAR, LED BY STRONG GROWTH IN NORTH AMERICA RETAIL AND PET.GENERAL MILLS INC - Q4 CONSTANT-CURRENCY ADJUSTED OPERATING PROFIT IS EXPECTED TO GROW FASTER THAN ORGANIC NET SALES.GENERAL MILLS INC - EXPECTS TO EXCEED FULL-YEAR FISCAL 2020 GUIDANCE RANGES OF 1 TO 2 PERCENT ORGANIC NET SALES GROWTH.GENERAL MILLS INC - EXPECTS TO EXCEED FY FISCAL 2020 GUIDANCE RANGES OF 4 TO 6 PERCENT GROWTH IN CONSTANT-CURRENCY ADJUSTED OPERATING PROFIT.GENERAL MILLS - EXPECTS TO EXCEED FY FISCAL 2020 GUIDANCE RANGES OF 6 TO 8 PERCENT GROWTH IN CONSTANT-CURRENCY ADJUSTED DILUTED EARNINGS PER SHARE.'}{'symbol': 'IFF', 'date': '2020-05-11 11:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'International Flavors & Fragrances Reports Additional Director Appointees', 'text': 'INTERNATIONAL FLAVORS & FRAGRANCES INC - ANNOUNCES ADDITIONAL DIRECTOR APPOINTEES FOR FUTURE BOARD OF DIRECTORS.INTERNATIONAL FLAVORS & FRAGRANCES INC - COMPANIES CONTINUE TO EXPECT THAT TRANSACTION WILL CLOSE IN Q1 OF 2021..INTERNATIONAL FLAVORS & FRAGRANCES - ORGANIZATION WILL INCLUDE FOUR DIVISIONS: TASTE, FOOD & BEVERAGE,  SCENT, HEALTH & BIOSCIENCES PHARMA, SOLUTIONS.INTERNATIONAL FLAVORS & FRAGRANCES INC - MATTHIAS HEINZEL WILL BE APPOINTED TO JOIN BOARD OF DIRECTORS OF IFF.INTERNATIONAL FLAVORS & FRAGRANCES INC - CAROL DAVIDSON WILL ALSO BE APPOINTED TO JOIN BOARD OF DIRECTORS OF FUTURE COMBINED COMPANY.'}{'symbol': 'MAR', 'date': '2020-05-11 15:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Marriott CEO Says Some Hotels Scheduled To Open In 2020 Will Get Delayed', 'text': 'MARRIOTT CEO SAYS SOME HOTELS SCHEDULED TO OPEN IN 2020 WILL GET DELAYED .MARRIOTT CEO SAYS NEGATIVE TRENDS APPEAR TO HAVE BOTTOMED AROUND THE WORLD - CONF CALL.MARRIOTT CEO SAYS RECOVERY IN DEMAND WILL NOT HAPPEN UNIFORMLY ACROSS ALL GEOGRAPHIES - CONF CALL.MARRIOTT CEO SAYS BILL MARRIOTT TO TRANSITION TO THE ROLE OF CHAIR EMERITUS IN 2022 - CONF CALL.MARRIOTT CEO SAYS DAVID MARRIOTT TO JOIN BOARD NEXT YEAR - CONF CALL.MARRIOTT CEO SAYS APRIL SEEM TO HAVE DEFINED THE BOTTOM; TRENDLINE NOW IS TOWARDS MORE HOTEL OPENINGS, NOT CLOSINGS - CONF CALL.MARRIOTT CEO SAYS CHINA APPEARS TO BE RECOVERING AND HOLDING.MARRIOTT CEO SAYS EUROPE IS MORE DEPENDENT ON LONG-HAUL TRAVEL COMPARED WITH CHINA AND NORTH AMERICA; EUROPE MARKET IS LIKELY TO BE THE SLOWEST TO RECOVER.MARRIOTT CEO SAYS HAS SEEN OCCUPANCY IN THE UNITED STATES TICK UP MARGINALLY IN THE PAST FEW WEEKS.MARRIOTT CEO SAYS LIKELY TO HAVE LESS FOOD AND BEVERAGE SERVICE IN EARLY STAGES OF HOTEL REOPENINGS.MARRIOTT CEO SAYS AN ECONOMIC HANGOVER IS POSSIBLE WHEN COVID-19 RECEDES.'}{'symbol': 'MAR', 'date': '2020-05-11 10:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Marriott International Reports First Quarter 2020 Results', 'text': 'MARRIOTT INTERNATIONAL REPORTS FIRST QUARTER 2020 RESULTS.Q1 ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.26.Q1 EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.09.Q1 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $0.80 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.MARRIOTT - Q1 2020 COMPARABLE SYSTEMWIDE CONSTANT DOLLAR REVPAR DECLINED 22.5 PERCENT WORLDWIDE.MARRIOTT - ADDED MORE THAN 14,500 ROOMS GLOBALLY DURING Q1.MARRIOTT - CURRENTLY, ROUGHLY A QUARTER OF OUR WORLDWIDE HOTELS ARE CLOSED.MARRIOTT - IN APRIL, WORLDWIDE REVPAR DECLINED ABOUT 90%.MARRIOTT - "SEEING AN UPTICK IN OWNER INTEREST IN DISCUSSING CONVERSIONS TO OUR BRANDS".MARRIOTT - RECOGNIZED NO INCENTIVE MANAGEMENT FEES IN 2020 Q1.MARRIOTT - OCCUPANCY AT HOTELS IN GREATER CHINA REACHED 25% IN APRIL.MARRIOTT - QTRLY TOTAL REVENUES $4,681 MILLION VERSUS $5,012 MILLION REPORTED LAST YEAR.MARRIOTT - OCCUPANCY AT HOTELS IN GREATER CHINA REACHED 25% IN APRIL, UP FROM LESS THAN 10% IN MID-FEBRUARY 2020.MARRIOTT - Q1 REPORTED & ADJUSTED EPS INCLUDED IMPAIRMENT CHARGES, BAD DEBT EXPENSE, AND GUARANTEE RESERVES OF $0.45 AND $0.42, RESPECTIVELY.MARRIOTT - EXPECT COVID-19\'S IMPACT WILL LIKELY RESULT IN SIGNIFICANTLY LOWER NEW ROOM OPENINGS THAN CO HAD BUDGETED FOR 2020.MARRIOTT - IN Q1, INCURRED $15 MILLION OF EXPENSES, RECOGNIZED $17 MILLION OF INSURANCE RECOVERIES RELATED TO DATA SECURITY INCIDENT DISCLOSED IN NOV. 2018.'}{'symbol': 'PENN', 'date': '2020-05-11 10:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Penn National Gaming Reports Public Offering Of Common Stock And Convertible Senior Notes Due 2026', 'text': 'PENN NATIONAL GAMING ANNOUNCES PUBLIC OFFERING OF COMMON STOCK AND CONVERTIBLE SENIOR NOTES DUE 2026.PENN NATIONAL GAMING INC -  COMMENCED $250 MILLION COMMON STOCK OFFERING AND $250 MILLION OFFERING OF CONVERTIBLE SENIOR NOTES DUE 2026.'}{'symbol': 'PFE', 'date': '2020-05-11 10:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Mylan Reports First Quarter 2020 Results And Reaffirms 2020 Guidance', 'text': "MYLAN REPORTS FIRST QUARTER 2020 RESULTS AND REAFFIRMS 2020 GUIDANCE.Q1 REVENUE ROSE 5 PERCENT TO $2.62 BILLION.Q1 TOTAL REVENUES OF $2.62 BILLION, UP 5%, UP 8% ON A CONSTANT CURRENCY BASIS, COMPARED TO PRIOR YEAR PERIOD..Q1 NORTH AMERICA SEGMENT NET SALES OF $955.5 MILLION, UP 4% ON AN ACTUAL AND CONSTANT CURRENCY BASIS.QTRLY EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.04.CURRENTLY DEVELOPING DETAILS RESTRUCTURING PROGRAM, INCLUDING WORKFORCE ACTIONS AND OTHER RESTRUCTURING ACTIVITIES.DELAYED IMPLEMENTATION OF 2020 RESTRUCTURING PROGRAM..Q1 REVENUE VIEW $2.64 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.REMAIN ON TRACK TO CLOSE PENDING COMBINATION WITH PFIZER'S UPJOHN BUSINESS IN SECOND HALF OF 2020.AT THIS TIME, CO DOES NOT FORESEE ANY SUPPLY DISRUPTIONS.CONTINUE TO TARGET APPROXIMATELY $1 BILLION OF DEBT REPAYMENT DURING 2020.ALL OF CO'S MANUFACTURING FACILITIES ARE CURRENTLY OPERATIONAL.AT THIS TIME, CO HAS SUFFICIENT SAFETY STOCK TO ADDRESS CURRENT NEEDS..CURRENTLY ARE NOT EXPERIENCING ANY SIGNIFICANT NEGATIVE IMPACT ON OVERALL GLOBAL DEMAND TRENDS.DO NOT SEE ANY NEGATIVE LIQUIDITY TRENDS RELATED TO COVID-19 PANDEMIC.INVENTORY LEVELS REMAIN IN-LINE WITH NORMAL LEVELS AND ARE CURRENTLY ASSESSED TO BE SUFFICIENT FOR ANTICIPATED DEMAND.DONATING 10 MILLION TABLETS OF HYDROXYCHLOROQUINE SULFATE TO HHS.DONATING HYDROXYCHLOROQUINE SULFATE TABLETS TO WORLD HEALTH ORGANIZATION.BELIEVE THAT CURRENTLY HAVE, AND WILL MAINTAIN, ABILITY TO MEET FORESEEABLE LIQUIDITY NEEDS."}{'symbol': 'PXD', 'date': '2020-05-11 10:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Pioneer Natural Resources Reports Offering Of Convertible Senior Notes Due 2025', 'text': 'PIONEER NATURAL RESOURCES ANNOUNCES OFFERING OF CONVERTIBLE SENIOR NOTES DUE 2025.PIONEER NATURAL RESOURCES - INTENDS TO OFFER $1.0 BILLION AGGREGATE PRINCIPAL AMOUNT OF CONVERTIBLE SENIOR NOTES DUE 2025.PIONEER NATURAL RESOURCES CO - NOTES WILL BE SENIOR UNSECURED OBLIGATIONS OF COMPANY..PIONEER NATURAL RESOURCES - EXPECTS TO USE PORTION OF NET PROCEEDS FROM OFFERING TO PAY COST OF CAPPED CALL TRANSACTIONS.PIONEER NATURAL RESOURCES - EXPECTS TO ENTER INTO CAPPED CALL TRANSACTIONS WITH ONE OR MORE OF INITIAL PURCHASERS OF NOTES.'}{'symbol': 'PG', 'date': '2020-05-11 12:30:00-04:56', 'title': "UK's CMA Launches Inquiry Into Pharm-A-Care Laboratories/Haliborange Business Of P&G Deal", 'text': 'LAUNCH OF INQUIRY INTO ACQUISITION BY PHARM-A-CARE LABORATORIES OF HALIBORANGE BUSINESS OF PROCTER & GAMBLE BY NOTICE TO PARTIES ON 11 MAY.'}{'symbol': 'PHM', 'date': '2020-05-11 09:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Pultegroup, Inc. Provides Update On Covid-19 Impacts And Response Actions', 'text': 'PULTEGROUP, INC. PROVIDES UPDATE ON COVID-19 IMPACTS AND RESPONSE ACTIONS.PULTEGROUP INC - TAKEN STEPS TO REDUCE TARGETED OVERHEAD EXPENSE THROUGH A COMBINATION OF LAYOFFS, FURLOUGHS.PULTEGROUP INC - ANTICIPATES TAKING A Q2 CHARGE OF ABOUT $10 MILLION FOR SEVERANCE AND RELATED EXPENSES.PULTEGROUP INC - AFTER AN INITIAL SIGNIFICANT CONTRACTION IN HOUSING DEMAND, RECENT SALES TRENDS HAVE BEEN MORE ENCOURAGING.PULTEGROUP INC - WEEKLY NET NEW ORDERS WENT FROM ABOUT 140 HOMES IN LAST WEEK OF MARCH TO ALMOST 400 HOMES IN FINAL FULL WEEK OF APRIL.PULTEGROUP INC - NET NEW ORDERS FOR MONTH OF APRIL WERE STILL DOWN APPROXIMATELY 50% FROM PRIOR YEAR.'}{'symbol': 'LUV', 'date': '2020-05-11 23:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'BOC Aviation Says Unit To Purchase 10 Boeing 737-8 Aircraft From Southwest Airlines Co', 'text': 'BOC AVIATION- UNIT TO PURCHASE 10 BOEING 737-8 AIRCRAFT FROM SOUTHWEST AIRLINES CO.'}{'symbol': 'TSLA', 'date': '2020-05-11 10:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Autonation CEO Mike Johnson Says Company Furloughed 7000 Workers- CNBC', 'text': ':AUTONATION CEO MIKE JOHNSON SAYS COMPANY FURLOUGHED 7000 WORKERS'}{'symbol': 'TMO', 'date': '2020-05-11 10:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Thermo Fisher Scientific To Double Its Capacity Of Viral Vector Manufacturing', 'text': "THERMO FISHER SCIENTIFIC TO DOUBLE ITS CAPACITY OF VIRAL VECTOR MANUFACTURING.THERMO FISHER SCIENTIFIC INC - $180 MILLION PROJECT WILL MORE THAN DOUBLE CO'S COMMERCIAL VIRAL VECTOR CAPACITY.THERMO FISHER SCIENTIFIC INC - NEW PLAINVILLE, MASSACHUSETTS, SITE WILL ACCELERATE COMMERCIALIZATION OF CELL AND GENE THERAPIES.THERMO FISHER SCIENTIFIC INC - CONSTRUCTION OF NEW 290,000-SQUARE-FOOT FACILITY IS EXPECTED TO BE COMPLETED IN 2022."}{'symbol': 'UAA', 'date': '2020-05-11 14:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Under Armour Expects Q2 Revenue To Be Down 50% To 60%', 'text': 'UNDER ARMOUR EXEC- COVID-19 CONTINUES TO CAUSE LARGE IMPACTS AND DISRUPTIONS ON DEMAND, SUPPLY DUE TO FACTORY CLOSURES - CONF CALL.UNDER ARMOUR EXEC- ALL OWNED AND WHOLESALE LOCATIONS IN CHINA HAVE REOPENED.UNDER ARMOUR EXEC-  E-COMMERCE BUSINESS HAS SHOWN STRENGTH SINCE START OF Q2.UNDER ARMOUR EXEC-  Q2 REVENUE EXPECTED TO BE DOWN 50% TO 60%.'}{'symbol': 'UAA', 'date': '2020-05-11 10:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Under Armour Reports Q1 2020 Results', 'text': 'UNDER ARMOUR REPORTS FIRST QUARTER 2020 RESULTS AND HIGHLIGHTS EFFORTS TO MANAGE THROUGH IMPACTS OF COVID-19.Q1 REVENUE $930 MILLION VERSUS REFINITIV IBES ESTIMATE OF $949 MILLION.Q1 ADJUSTED LOSS PER SHARE $0.34.Q1 LOSS PER SHARE $1.30.Q1 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $-0.19 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.QTRLY RESTRUCTURING AND IMPAIRMENT CHARGES WERE $436 MILLION CONSISTING OF $301 MILLION IN RESTRUCTURING AND RELATED IMPAIRMENT CHARGES.TEMPORARILY LAYING OFF TEAMMATES THAT WORKED IN OWNED RETAIL STORES AND U.S.-BASED DISTRIBUTION CENTERS..TIGHTENING HIRING, CONTRACT SERVICES AND TRAVEL AND OTHER DISCRETIONARY AND VARIABLE COSTS..TAKING ACTIONS TO LIMIT BROADER MARKETING ACTIVATIONS UNTIL CO HAS GREATER VISIBILITY INTO MAGNITUDE OF VIRUS IMPACT.EXPECTING TO REDUCE ORIGINALLY PLANNED 2020 OPERATING EXPENSES BY APPROXIMATELY $325 MILLION.ENDED QUARTER WITH INVENTORY UP 7 PERCENT TO $940 MILLION..PROACTIVELY REDUCING PLANNED INVENTORY RECEIPTS.QTRLY GROSS MARGIN INCREASED 110 BASIS POINTS TO 46.3 PERCENT.IN PROCESS OF AMENDING CREDIT AGREEMENT, WHICH IS ON TRACK TO CLOSE TUESDAY.ENDED THE FIRST QUARTER WITH CASH AND CASH EQUIVALENTS OF $959 MILLION.QUANTIFICATION OF NEGATIVE IMPACTS ON FINANCIAL AND OPERATING RESULTS CANNOT REASONABLY BE ESTIMATED AT THIS TIME.TRAFFIC IN CHINA, WHILE RECOVERING STEADILY IN RECENT WEEKS, CONTINUES TO BE DOWN YEAR-OVER-YEAR..BUSINESS RESULTS AND TRENDS IN SOUTH KOREA HAVE BEEN SIMILAR TO THOSE IN CHINA.'}{'symbol': 'ZBH', 'date': '2020-05-11 11:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Zimmer Biomet Reports First Quarter 2020 Financial Results', 'text': 'ZIMMER BIOMET ANNOUNCES FIRST QUARTER 2020 FINANCIAL RESULTS.Q1 ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.70.Q1 LOSS PER SHARE $2.46.Q1 SALES $1.784 BILLION VERSUS REFINITIV IBES ESTIMATE OF $1.79 BILLION.Q1 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $1.38 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.ZIMMER BIOMET HOLDINGS - SEES DECLINE IN ELECTIVE PROCEDURE VOLUMES IN FINAL WEEKS OF Q1 CONTINUING TO HAVE SIGNIFICANT NEGATIVE IMPACT IN Q2.UNABLE TO QUANTIFY EXPECTED IMPACT OF COVD-19 ON RESULTS.NOT PROVIDING FY FINANCIAL GUIDANCE.'}